# The paths that matter most: the trust boundary (credentials, the extension
# host, the network surface) and CI itself. Every path resolves to the same
# owner through the wildcard below. This is a map for reviewers, not a gate:
# branch protection requires the check names and no review, and
# `scripts/guard.sh` fails when a path listed here stops existing.

*                     @fschrhunt

/crates/core/src/extensions/        @fschrhunt
/crates/core/src/resources/packages.rs @fschrhunt
/crates/core/src/resources/packages/ @fschrhunt
/crates/core/src/auth/       @fschrhunt
/crates/core/src/config/     @fschrhunt
/crates/core/src/providers/  @fschrhunt
/crates/core/src/session.rs  @fschrhunt
/crates/core/src/tools/      @fschrhunt
/crates/core/src/update.rs   @fschrhunt
/crates/www/                @fschrhunt
# The guides are the source for three readers — GitHub, the website, and the
# binary's `ulo docs` — so their structure, front matter, and links are reviewed
# like code. docs/README.md is the contract and crates/cli/tests/docs.rs enforces it; a new
# folder is a navigation change, not an edit.
/docs/                @fschrhunt
/contributing/        @fschrhunt
/.github/             @fschrhunt
/scripts/guard.sh     @fschrhunt
/install.sh           @fschrhunt
